              "isVerified": false
            },
            "content": "As models get more capable, they become more dangerous. As they become more dangerous, these companies argue for tighter access. The better the model gets, the stronger the case for never releasing it.\n\nAnthropic is using the \"dangerous\" private version to do research, find vulnerabilities, and publish the results as proof of how advanced it is. The capability is \"too dangerous\" when the public wants access, but a major achievement when Anthropic uses it.\n\nThese models will shape research, education, finance, software, weapons, robotics, media, and government.\n\nThere are almost no meaningful checks on this. Anthropic decides what counts as dangerous, who gets access, and whether Anthropic's own safety claims are justified. There are no clear public rules, no real outside audit, and no consequence if \"safety\" is being used to protect Anthropic's moat.\n\nThis is not going to end well for humanity.",
            "createdAt": "Tue Jul 28 22:55:52 +0000 2026",
